|~ `::host`, the host a session is in, and what is declared under it: its
   page, which the host writes, its screen, the kinds that lie on it and
   what the reader declared.
   The rules it holds: [QSNAM#binding], [QSSLF#page], [D476]. ~|

:host
  |~~ The host a session is in, the program that embeds the language: one
      name in every host, whose page the host writes, the page of the
      program, which a source of the host declares alone,
      `:host |~~ … ~~|;`. `::host | status` answers its screen, the
      sections of its state, `::host | kinds` the kinds that lie on it and
      `::host | env` what the reader declared, each asked of `::host` at
      the head of a query. Where no host wrote a page this one stands, the
      language alone embedded.
      ::link~(::host/status) ::link~(::host/kinds) ::link~(::host/env)
      ::link~(::qlang/hosts)
  ~~|
  ::kind
    | accepts |~~ No value: `::host` names the host a session is in. ~~| #[]
    | throws :PayloadKindNotTakenError
        |~~ `::host` names the host a session is in, its page and its
            words, and takes no payload: it is asked by itself,
            `::host | doc`.
        ~~|
    | proves :PayloadKindNotTakenError/refusesAValue
        |~~ No value is put under `::host`. ~~|
        ~(5 | tag ::host !| tag | eq ::host/PayloadKindNotTakenError);

:host/status
  |~~ Answers the screen of the host a session is in, its state in
      sections, each a snippet the host declares under `::host` with its
      page, `:host/budget |~~ The budget of an answer. ~~| ::snippet~(…);`:
      a section holds the address that names it, the prose of its page,
      the query that takes it again and what that query answers now, a
      failure as its error at rest. A host that declares no section
      answers none, the language alone among them.
      ::link~(::snippet) ::link~(::host)
  ~~|
  ::fn
    | on |~~ The host itself, `::host`. ~~| ::tag
    | returns
        |~~ The sections, each `{:section … :page … :query … :answer …}`,
            in the order of their addresses.
        ~~|
        ::vec
    | throws :ArgsBeyondInputsError
        |~~ `status` answers every section and takes none: one is read by
            its address, `::host | status | filter ~(get /section | eq ::host/budget)`.
        ~~|
    | proves :answersNoSectionOfTheLanguageAlone
        |~~ The language alone declares no section. ~~|
        ~(::host | status | eq [])
    | proves :ArgsBeyondInputsError/refusesASection
        |~~ A section given to `status` is refused under the verb. ~~|
        ~(::host | status :budget !| tag | eq ::host/status/ArgsBeyondInputsError)
    | impl ~(manifest | toVec | filter ~(binding | value | tag | eq ::snippet)
            | map ~(get {:section ~(it) :page ~(doc | content) :query ~(binding | value | payload) :answer ~(binding | value | answer !| it)}));

:host/kinds
  |~~ Answers the set of the labels the scope reads, the kinds declared
      under a name, each by its tag name: those the language and the host
      declared, the topic of the language and `::host` among them, and
      those the reader declares. A query asks which kinds there are before
      it asks one of them for its page, `::set | doc`, or for what lies
      under it, `::set | manifest`. A chapter a topic tells is no kind:
      `::qlang/values` is a page `doc` reads, which `manifest` of its
      topic lists. It is asked of `::host` and takes no kind.
      ::link~(::host/env) ::link~(::qlang)
  ~~|
  ::fn
    | on |~~ The host itself, `::host`. ~~| ::tag
    | returns |~~ The tag names of the kinds the scope reads. ~~| ::set
    | throws :ArgsBeyondInputsError
        |~~ `kinds` answers every kind and takes none: whether a kind is
            there is `::host | kinds | has ::set`.
        ~~|
    | proves :holdsTheKindsOfTheLanguage
        |~~ The kinds of the language are read. ~~|
        ~(::host | kinds | has ::vec)
    | proves :holdsTheTopic
        |~~ The topic of the language is a label too. ~~|
        ~(::host | kinds | has ::qlang)
    | proves :holdsAReadersKind
        |~~ A kind the reader declares is read. ~~|
        ~(:Box |~~ A box. ~~|; ::host | kinds | has ::Box)
    | proves :holdsNoChapter
        |~~ A chapter of the topic is no kind. ~~|
        ~(::host | kinds | has ::qlang/values | not)
    | proves :refusesAnotherSubject
        |~~ A value is no host: `kinds` of it is refused as a verb no kind
            of the value answers, naming its address.
        ~~|
        ~([1 2] | kinds !| get [~(tag) ~(addresses)] | eq [::call/KindAnswersNoVerbError #[::host/kinds]])
    | proves :ArgsBeyondInputsError/refusesAKind
        |~~ A kind given to `kinds` is refused under the verb. ~~|
        ~(::host | kinds ::set !| tag | eq ::host/kinds/ArgsBeyondInputsError)
    | impl ::builtin{};

:host/env
  |~~ Answers what the reader declared before the step, the cells of a
      session before it among them: a map from each name to the record of
      its binding, `::binding` with its name, its docs, its value, its
      source and its origin. `:Box |~~ A box. ~~|; ::host | env` answers the
      record of `:Box`, and `::host | env | get /Box` hands it to the next
      step. A name with a path is held by its address. Inside a fork it
      holds the names before the fork and the fork's own, and the fork's
      stay inside it, and so does code a step wrote; code held as data
      holds its own and the nodes and the labels of the step that runs it,
      a value the reader named withheld from it. What the language and the
      host declared stands apart, so at the start of a query it answers
      `{}`: `::host | kinds` lists their kinds, and `manifest` what lies
      under a noun. It is asked of `::host` and takes no name.
      ::link~(::any/binding) ::link~(::host/kinds)
  ~~|
  ::fn
    | on |~~ The host itself, `::host`. ~~| ::tag
    | returns
        |~~ The records of what the reader declared, by name. ~~|
        ::map
    | throws :ArgsBeyondInputsError
        |~~ `env` answers every name the reader declared and takes none:
            one record is read by its key, `::host | env | get /Box`.
        ~~|
    | proves :holdsADeclaredName
        |~~ A name declared before the step is held. ~~|
        ~(:number/double ~(mul 2); ::host | env | has :number/double)
    | proves :holdsTheRecord
        |~~ Each name holds the record its declaration wrote. ~~|
        ~(:number/double ~(mul 2); ::host | env | get /:number/double | value | eq ~(mul 2))
    | proves :holdsANameWithAPath
        |~~ A name with a path is held by its address. ~~|
        ~(:Box |~~ A box. ~~|; :Box/area ~(1); ::host | env | keys | eq #[:Box :Box/area])
    | proves :holdsTheNamesOfAForkAndKeepsThemInside
        |~~ Inside a fork the names before it and its own are held, and
            the fork's stay inside it.
        ~~|
        ~(:Box |~~ A box. ~~|; get [~(:Crate |~~ A crate. ~~|; ::host | env | keys) ~(::host | env | keys)] | eq [#[:Box :Crate] #[:Box]])
    | proves :isEmptyAtTheStart
        |~~ Nothing is declared at the start. ~~|
        ~(::host | env | eq {})
    | proves :refusesAnotherSubject
        |~~ A value is no host: `env` of it is refused as a verb no kind of
            the value answers, naming its address.
        ~~|
        ~([1 2] | env !| get [~(tag) ~(addresses)] | eq [::call/KindAnswersNoVerbError #[::host/env]])
    | proves :ArgsBeyondInputsError/refusesAName
        |~~ A name given to `env` is refused under the verb. ~~|
        ~(:Box |~~ A box. ~~|; ::host | env :Box !| tag | eq ::host/env/ArgsBeyondInputsError)
    | impl ::builtin{};
